  "notes": "{苦|くる}しい expresses pain, difficulty, or distress.\n\nFORMS:\n- {苦|くる}しい (dictionary form)\n- {苦|くる}しく (adverb: painfully)\n- {苦|くる}しさ (noun: pain, difficulty)\n- {苦|くる}しがる (to show signs of pain)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {息|いき}が{苦|くる}しい (hard to breathe)\n- {生活|せいかつ}が{苦|くる}しい (life is hard financially)\n- {苦|くる}しい{立場|たちば} (difficult position)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {苦|くる}しい: painful, distressing\n- {辛|つら}い: hard, tough (emotionally)\n- {痛|いた}い: painful (physical)\n- {難|むずか}しい: difficult (intellectually)",
